# Browser key for Google Photorealistic 3D Tiles (Map Tiles API).
# Enables the Cesium Florida campus map and the in-tour aerial 3D view.
#
# Google Cloud setup:
#   1. Enable **Map Tiles API** (Photorealistic 3D Tiles). Billing required.
#   2. Optionally enable Geocoding API, Maps Embed API, Street View Static API
#      (existing campus-tour features).
#   3. Create an API key and restrict it:
#        Application: HTTP referrers
#          https://banksy1224.github.io/*
#          https://www.keiseruniversity.edu/*
#          http://localhost:5173/*          (local Vite)
#        APIs: Map Tiles API (+ the optional APIs above)
#   4. Do not commit a real key. This value ships in the client bundle.
#
# Local:   copy this file to `.env.local` and paste the key.
# Deploy:  GitHub repo secret `VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY` (see deploy.yml).
# Alias:   `GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY` is also read (same value).
#
# Without a key, Florida shows a clear in-app message and the stylized 3D
# peninsula; campus tours stay on the stylized scene.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Optional: enables the AI concierge ("Ask the guide").
# Set to your deployed backend URL (see server/README.md), e.g.
# https://your-app.up.railway.app . Without it, the concierge stays hidden.
VITE_AI_ENDPOINT=

# Optional: GitHub Pages static path for the two-step TCPA "Request info" sheet.
# Get a free access key at https://web3forms.com (public-safe in the client).
# Deploy: add a GitHub repo VARIABLE named VITE_WEB3FORMS_KEY.
# The sheet ALSO POSTs /api/rfi when a backend is present (relative, or
# ${VITE_AI_ENDPOINT}/api/rfi on Railway).
VITE_WEB3FORMS_KEY=

# Optional: mailto: fallback inbox when no Web3Forms key and no backend.
VITE_LEAD_EMAIL=
